summary, not a substitute for those texts.


agent-desktop
-------------
  Used for:  the native desktop engine behind Biorouter Copilot
  Licence:   Apache License 2.0
  Copyright: published by Vercel Labs; upstream states no copyright line and
             ships no NOTICE file
  Upstream:  https://github.com/vercel-labs/agent-desktop
  Version:   1.3.1, pinned at commit b0b7277bea09b770ef9d1fb45aad667bc432cd57
  Licence text and dependency list:
    in this repository   vendor/agent-desktop/{LICENSE,DEPENDENCIES.txt}
    in an installed app  beside the helper binary, inside the payload, as
                         LICENSE.agent-desktop and DEPENDENCIES.agent-desktop.txt

  Biorouter ships agent-desktop unmodified. The upstream source the build
  reads is vendored at vendor/agent-desktop/source, checked file by file
  against a hash manifest before every build, and no Biorouter patch is
  applied to it; Biorouter's own rules live in its own code around the
  binary. On macOS the unmodified binary is placed in an app bundle named
  Biorouter Copilot, with Biorouter's bundle identifier and signature.

  The build copies upstream's LICENSE and the dependency list into the
  shipped payload and records their checksums in the payload manifest, and
  the verify step fails the build if the manifest and the files on disk
  disagree, or if the licence is not upstream's text.

  The helper is compiled from crates.io crates locked in upstream's
  Cargo.lock: 141 of the 160 it locks reach at least one shipped target. Their
  licences, counted over those 141: MIT OR Apache-2.0 (and its other
  spellings) 108, MIT 21, Apache-2.0 3, Unlicense OR MIT 2, MIT OR Zlib OR
  Apache-2.0 2, Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception OR Apache-2.0 OR MIT 2,
  0BSD OR MIT OR Apache-2.0 1, (MIT OR Apache-2.0) AND Unicode-3.0 1, and
  Zlib 1 (zlib-rs). DEPENDENCIES.txt lists every crate with its version,
  licence and the targets that compile it; each crate's source, with its
  licence text, is published at https://crates.io/crates/<crate>/<version>.


